Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day. By 4 October the desk had
**412 reports**, merged as one ticket. They are not one bug. The kb logic splits them into two
problems, one per cause. The desk has now worked both.

## The two causes

- **#1 — Date parser flips day-first tenants' dates.** 379 reports. The shared parser reads every
  date month first; a day-first tenant's `DD/MM/YYYY` comes out flipped.
- **#2 — booking-v3 form hint misreads day-first tenants' dates.** 33 reports. The form prints
  `MM/DD/YYYY` and reads the tenant's typed date that way; only the three booking-v3 tenants hit it.

## Lessons

- A merged ticket can hold more than one cause. Count by cause, not by subject.
- The tenant's booking form decides which bug a report is, not the intake tag.

